00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:04.880
W pociagu jest tlok, Crowded

00:08:04.891 --> 00:08:05.891
Train.

00:08:06.691 --> 00:08:09.061
It is a very special song

00:08:09.181 --> 00:08:11.400
which helped people make

00:08:11.581 --> 00:08:13.821
a living, even survive.

00:08:14.971 --> 00:08:17.791
But the origin of this song is

00:08:17.881 --> 00:08:20.071
not in Polish language and

00:08:20.401 --> 00:08:21.871
not in Polish culture.

00:08:22.471 --> 00:08:25.600
The origins comes to, back

00:08:25.760 --> 00:08:27.320
to Latin America,

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:29.960
Mexico, where

00:08:30.120 --> 00:08:33.000
it was called Cielito Lindo,

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:36.000
and it was a folk

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:39.120
song belonging to the copla genre,

00:08:39.400 --> 00:08:41.290
and performed by

00:08:42.670 --> 00:08:45.099
mariachi wandering bands

00:08:45.610 --> 00:08:46.829
during that time.

00:08:46.990 --> 00:08:49.810
And it was popularized

00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:53.050
by the composer Quirino

00:08:53.780 --> 00:08:56.690
Mendoza y Cortes in the late 19th century.

00:08:57.070 --> 00:08:59.709
He used this melody for

00:08:59.710 --> 00:09:02.680
his composition, The Wrestler,

00:09:03.490 --> 00:09:04.862
and from that time it became

00:09:06.250 --> 00:09:07.599
enormously popular

00:09:08.710 --> 00:09:10.229
in Mexico, in different Spanish

00:09:11.350 --> 00:09:13.959
culture, diasporas in the world, but very

00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:16.479
soon also in other

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:17.960
cultures as well.

00:09:17.980 --> 00:09:19.205
So the song was performed

00:09:20.530 --> 00:09:21.608
by such famous singers

00:09:23.140 --> 00:09:25.180
like Placido Domingo,

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:28.989
Luciano Pavarotti, in Poland

00:09:28.990 --> 00:09:31.270
by famous singers

00:09:31.540 --> 00:09:33.790
Violetta Villas or

00:09:33.910 --> 00:09:36.000
Maryla Rodowicz,

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:40.600
who performed it

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:43.589
under the title Long Living

00:09:43.590 --> 00:09:46.080
the Ball, or Dancing Party, which

00:09:46.240 --> 00:09:49.060
became a very popular

00:09:49.960 --> 00:09:52.839
song during the communist time in Poland.

00:09:53.890 --> 00:09:56.499
But when it came

00:09:56.500 --> 00:09:58.560
to Poland in the thirties

00:09:59.410 --> 00:10:01.740
of the last century, via

00:10:02.020 --> 00:10:03.020
Berlin,

00:10:04.660 --> 00:10:06.999
and it was sang by

00:10:09.360 --> 00:10:10.920
a famous

00:10:11.080 --> 00:10:12.370
Chilean singer

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:15.399
at that time,

00:10:17.020 --> 00:10:18.429
Rosita Serrano,

00:10:19.390 --> 00:10:21.220
who came to Berlin

00:10:22.420 --> 00:10:24.549
singing it,

00:10:24.840 --> 00:10:27.949
she was called Chilean Nightingale,

00:10:28.260 --> 00:10:30.480
a famous singer, and that, that

00:10:30.680 --> 00:10:33.080
was the

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:35.830
way how it came from Berlin

00:10:35.930 --> 00:10:37.880
to prewar Warsaw.

00:10:38.090 --> 00:10:40.360
It was time of depression, a time

00:10:40.440 --> 00:10:42.219
of economic crisis.

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:44.729
So the lyrics to this song

00:10:46.170 --> 00:10:48.790
were in Polish, were

00:10:48.840 --> 00:10:51.900
about smuggling groceries

00:10:52.770 --> 00:10:55.800
in trains or trams

00:10:56.280 --> 00:10:57.280
in Warsaw.

00:10:58.140 --> 00:10:59.757
And this version of this song was

00:11:00.990 --> 00:11:02.166
forgotten in, in Poland.

00:11:02.790 --> 00:11:05.700
And I think thanks to the performance

00:11:05.910 --> 00:11:06.989
by Mr. Peretz

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:11.219
in that recording, we

00:11:11.220 --> 00:11:13.560
still can have these lyrics and this

00:11:13.590 --> 00:11:14.898
first version of Polish

00:11:18.960 --> 00:11:21.019
presence of, of this song

00:11:21.600 --> 00:11:22.770
at that time.

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:24.995
We may call these type of songs, we

00:11:25.800 --> 00:11:28.829
called contrafactum, which

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:31.319
means that there is

00:11:31.320 --> 00:11:33.689
a substitution of one

00:11:33.690 --> 00:11:35.189
takes to the another

00:11:36.990 --> 00:11:39.839
without any substantial change in music,

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:42.569
so keep the melody and change

00:11:42.960 --> 00:11:44.822
the lyrics according to circumstances,

00:11:45.660 --> 00:11:48.809
historical, political,
culture circumstances.

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:52.079
So when war

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:54.629
came to Warsaw,

00:11:55.470 --> 00:11:57.420
to Poland in

00:11:58.110 --> 00:11:59.110
1939, the lyrics

00:12:01.080 --> 00:12:03.599
changed and

00:12:03.600 --> 00:12:05.969
it was mostly about

00:12:05.970 --> 00:12:08.100
the war, "teraz jest wojna

00:12:08.430 --> 00:12:10.740
kto handluje ten zyje." "It is war

00:12:10.890 --> 00:12:13.349
now. Who sells,

00:12:13.710 --> 00:12:14.710
lives."

00:12:16.780 --> 00:12:17.780
And it was sung by

00:12:19.240 --> 00:12:21.760
the people on the streets

00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:24.570
who from one side, like Mr. Peretz

00:12:25.390 --> 00:12:28.120
who wanted to survive to make their living.

00:12:30.550 --> 00:12:31.677
From the other hand, it

00:12:33.010 --> 00:12:35.979
was sung by people who are engaged

00:12:35.980 --> 00:12:37.789
in underground movement.

00:12:38.260 --> 00:12:39.289
So it was still about

00:12:41.380 --> 00:12:44.049
smuggling, but not necessarily

00:12:44.050 --> 00:12:46.360
groceries, also weapons and

00:12:46.600 --> 00:12:48.469
illegal literature as well.

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:50.120
And because of that,

00:12:51.490 --> 00:12:53.889
it was sometimes very dangerous to

00:12:53.890 --> 00:12:56.419
be a singer of that songs,

00:12:56.440 --> 00:12:58.953
because many of them belonged

00:12:59.080 --> 00:13:01.719
to the underground movement and

00:13:01.720 --> 00:13:03.430
took part in actions

00:13:04.090 --> 00:13:05.799
against Nazi Germans

00:13:06.640 --> 00:13:07.929
during the occupation

00:13:09.050 --> 00:13:11.529
time. So we started to

00:13:11.530 --> 00:13:12.706
call that song

00:13:13.760 --> 00:13:15.040
Forbidden Songs.

00:13:15.200 --> 00:13:18.230
And this is a title of a famous

00:13:18.740 --> 00:13:21.260
movie, which was, I think

00:13:21.410 --> 00:13:23.899
the first feature movie after the war

00:13:23.900 --> 00:13:24.900
in Poland,

00:13:27.380 --> 00:13:29.720
created in 1947

00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:33.019
by the film director, a film

00:13:33.020 --> 00:13:35.600
director, Leonard Buczkowski,

00:13:35.720 --> 00:13:37.840
who established his

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:41.600
career before the war as a director

00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:43.920
of famous war

00:13:44.080 --> 00:13:46.599
movies. It was big budget

00:13:49.480 --> 00:13:52.089
and, and he

00:13:52.090 --> 00:13:54.760
cooperated after

00:13:54.920 --> 00:13:57.400
the war with Ludwik

00:13:57.560 --> 00:13:59.920
Starski for screenwriting, was an

00:13:59.990 --> 00:14:02.240
author of screen writing for

00:14:02.480 --> 00:14:03.480
this movie.

00:14:03.760 --> 00:14:05.919
Ludwik Starski was

00:14:06.340 --> 00:14:09.040
the father of a famous set

00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:12.440
designer set designer Allan Starski,

00:14:12.680 --> 00:14:15.499
who worked for many
years with Humphrey Bogart.

00:14:16.460 --> 00:14:18.620
And he was also

00:14:19.010 --> 00:14:21.500
awarded the Academy Award

00:14:21.650 --> 00:14:24.469
for Schindler's

00:14:24.470 --> 00:14:26.529
List in 1994.

00:14:28.130 --> 00:14:30.670
So they both, Buczkowski

00:14:30.680 --> 00:14:32.880
and Starski decided to

00:14:33.080 --> 00:14:35.000
make a song

00:14:35.200 --> 00:14:37.860
a hero of this

00:14:37.870 --> 00:14:38.870
film.

00:14:39.070 --> 00:14:41.139
So it is a plot, of course,

00:14:41.680 --> 00:14:44.469
around it about different

00:14:44.740 --> 00:14:46.959
underground activities in,

00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:50.380
in Warsaw during the occupation.

00:14:51.420 --> 00:14:54.790
But the main hero of this movie

00:14:55.060 --> 00:14:57.959
is a song, the Forgotten Songs,

00:14:57.970 --> 00:15:00.459
and among them,

00:15:00.760 --> 00:15:01.929
the Crowded Train.

00:15:03.310 --> 00:15:05.829
The communist authorities were

00:15:05.830 --> 00:15:08.349
not satisfied with the first version

00:15:08.350 --> 00:15:09.350
of this movie.

00:15:09.460 --> 00:15:11.371
It was not enough for them, politically

00:15:11.920 --> 00:15:13.959
engaged on the Soviet

00:15:15.130 --> 00:15:16.649
side, and not enough underlying

00:15:18.010 --> 00:15:19.240
the cruelty of

00:15:20.500 --> 00:15:21.969
the German soldiers.

00:15:21.970 --> 00:15:24.429
So that, after

00:15:24.520 --> 00:15:27.399
two years they made a second version

00:15:27.880 --> 00:15:29.860
of this movie.

00:15:30.340 --> 00:15:32.809
And, you know, it, it,

00:15:32.810 --> 00:15:35.199
it became a very, very

00:15:35.200 --> 00:15:36.200
famous

00:15:37.930 --> 00:15:40.860
film, which popular, popularizes

00:15:41.110 --> 00:15:43.779
this song, Crowded Train again.

00:15:44.350 --> 00:15:47.099
But this is not the end of the story.

00:15:48.750 --> 00:15:51.542
And this song has been long living.

00:15:52.140 --> 00:15:54.860
In fact, when we

00:15:54.870 --> 00:15:57.570
in Poland had a so-called martial law

00:15:58.380 --> 00:16:01.520
implemented by General Jaruzelski

00:16:01.840 --> 00:16:04.280
on December 13,

00:16:04.560 --> 00:16:05.920
1981,

00:16:08.130 --> 00:16:10.649
mostly people in Poland said

00:16:10.720 --> 00:16:12.720
there is another type of occupation.

00:16:12.730 --> 00:16:14.579
That's the war came back

00:16:15.270 --> 00:16:17.729
and it was a war within our

00:16:17.730 --> 00:16:19.799
society, but

00:16:20.160 --> 00:16:22.919
it was a good ground, a new context

00:16:22.980 --> 00:16:24.107
for for such songs from

00:16:25.440 --> 00:16:28.199
the war time and again

00:16:29.020 --> 00:16:31.919
Crowded Train became very popular

00:16:31.920 --> 00:16:32.998
at that time under, of

00:16:34.320 --> 00:16:35.320
course, the new

00:16:36.960 --> 00:16:38.381
title and with new lyrics now

00:16:39.690 --> 00:16:42.094
about Green Crow,

00:16:43.500 --> 00:16:46.640
Zielona Wrona, Wrona was an abbreviation

00:16:46.840 --> 00:16:49.800
of the government

00:16:50.120 --> 00:16:51.786
name, you know, in this new regime

00:16:52.280 --> 00:16:53.449
circumstances.

00:16:54.080 --> 00:16:56.959
So it was a new living for

00:16:57.710 --> 00:16:58.710
that song.

00:16:59.990 --> 00:17:00.990
And I wish

00:17:02.540 --> 00:17:05.149
that it would be not the

00:17:05.150 --> 00:17:07.009
end of the story.

00:17:08.660 --> 00:17:09.934
I wish that this song will

00:17:11.060 --> 00:17:13.000
survive in our

00:17:13.200 --> 00:17:15.390
cultural memory in archives

00:17:15.931 --> 00:17:18.420
and that

00:17:18.450 --> 00:17:20.610
this will influence new

00:17:21.361 --> 00:17:23.028
productions and performings.

00:17:23.641 --> 00:17:26.180
But my hope is that

00:17:26.281 --> 00:17:28.860
never again in connection

00:17:28.861 --> 00:17:31.335
with new wars in the future.

00:17:31.891 --> 00:17:34.380
Let's keep it for the peace time.

